  "notes": "The slowest and stillest entry in this batch, and the research gives it in one phrase: \"a beat ticking time.\" Metronomic and unfussy is `quantizeStrength` 0.97 with `velocityVar` 0.06 — the tightest pair on this axis — over a kick that plays 1 and the and-of-3 at `syncopation` 0.1, ghost notes at 0.03, swing flat at 0.5 and `percs.lanes` emptied entirely, because the drama is documented as living in the strings and the choir rather than in the kit. The harmony is the sustained minor string cycle of the Stevie Wonder interpolation: `i–v–i–VI` at the top weight over a pedal bass, with no functional cadence, which is why `voicing.register` is 40 semitones wide and the top voice moves stepwise. The choir is a chordal pad and not a hook, so it is the countermelody at the 0.3 floor rather than a second melody. The bass is the pedal — `mirror_kick` at 0.97 with glide at 0.02 and no passing tones, the most static bass here. The additive intro (strings, then choir, then drums) is an 8-to-16-bar intro against a near-zero `switchUpProb`: the record's tension is layer accumulation, not section contrast, and there is no bridge in the authored structure because the research says there is none. ⚠ `modes` are authored because the parent's Death Row moods pin 90–100 and this band is 78–92, which would have made the half-time-reading records unreachable. ⚠ `medium` per the research's medium-high. ⚠ **The countermelody reached only 961 distinct answers in 1000 seeds against a floor of 980**, so it was given range: densityRatio 0.45. A counter is combinatorial in the styles it may pick, its density against the melody, and the phrase length it answers inside — one style over a thin density inside a single phrase length has almost nothing a seed can vary.",
